  "description": "SUBVET crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C22 H72 Cr2 Dy5 O41 7+,7(Cl1 O4 1-),21(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1B (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.420-4.582 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.92-137.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5Cr2(H2L)2(OAc)6(μ3-OH)6(H2O)15](ClO4)7·21H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 15 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
